  [OK] lib/sbi/sbi_sse.c:544-605  sse_event_inject
      Core injection machinery correctly saves interrupted context: a6, a7, flags, sepc to event state (L553-556). Sets mepc to S-mode handler PC (L587), configures MPP=PRV_S (L594), clears virtualization bits MPV (L598-603), and sets SDT for supervisor-directed traps (L595). Also handles H-extension hstatus save/restore (L564-581). Register manipulation is thorough and correct. The function itself is not the gap.
  [RISK] lib/utils/irqchip/imsic.c:161-164  imsic_process_hwirqs
      The default case in the IMSIC handler switch prints and silently drops unhandled IRQs without any SSE injection. An unclassifiable interrupt arriving via IMSIC is logged via sbi_printf() but never surfaced to S-mode. This is a secondary blind spot: if a hardware fault manifests as an unrecognized IMSIC interrupt, the OS supervisor has zero visibility. Lower priority than the sbi_trap.c gap (which hangs the hart), but this path quietly discards error information. Depends on the implicit invariant that all legitimate IMSIC interrupts are enumerated in the switch cases.

